{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15410974","formula":"C₁₀H₁₃NO","hill":"C10H13NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":13.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Formetorex"},"descriptions":{"en":"Formetorex (INN), also known as formetamide or N-formylamphetamine, is a substituted amphetamine described as an anorectic which does not appear to have ever been marketed. Formetorex is also an intermediate in the production of amphetamine by the \"Leuckart reaction.\" It is also commonly found as an impurity in clandestine labs where this synthesis method is used. Due to the simplicity of the Leuckart reaction, it is the most popular synthetic route employed for the illicit manufacture of amphetamines."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":65614,"mass":163.22,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(CC1=CC=CC=C1)NC=O","inchikey":"SGSYPSYCGPLSML-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"N-(1-phenylpropan-2-yl)formamide","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"65614","atoms":25,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.894,"y":-2.007,"z":1.101,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.193,"y":-0.442,"z":-0.606,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.775,"y":0.757,"z":0.126,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.564,"y":1.394,"z":-0.579,"el":"C"},{"x":0.741,"y":0.69,"z":-0.296,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.969,"y":1.708,"z":0.215,"el":"C"},{"x":1.507,"y":1.089,"z":0.788,"el":"C"},{"x":1.149,"y":-0.344,"z":-1.124,"el":"C"},{"x":2.713,"y":0.439,"z":1.05,"el":"C"},{"x":2.354,"y":-0.995,"z":-0.861,"el":"C"},{"x":3.136,"y":-0.604,"z":0.226,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.206,"y":-1.684,"z":-0.038,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.499,"y":0.47,"z":1.149,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.462,"y":2.439,"z":-0.255,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.729,"y":1.444,"z":-1.664,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.817,"y":1.223,"z":0.71,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.301,"y":2.02,"z":-0.782,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.709,"y":2.605,"z":0.785,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.486,"y":-0.34,"z":-1.573,"el":"H"},{"x":1.185